The web-server folder contains the core backend application that handles HTTP requests and serves the React frontend, acting as the main entry point for the entire project's functionality. It manages all server-side operations including API endpoints, database connections, and request processing through Express.js framework. The folder's package.json, tsconfig.json, and tsconfig.tsbuildinfo files work together to configure the development environment, manage dependencies, and enable TypeScript compilation for the Node.js server.
